<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>To prepare for a backyard party, a parent uses two identical hoses to fill a small pool that is 15 inches deep and a large pool that is 27 inches deep.</para>
<para>The height of the water in each pool is a function of time since the water is turned on.</para>
<media><image alt="Two pools." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c466027622a96eb3bdb0f8fbbcb0c9a69dba861e"/></media><para>Here are descriptions of three situations. For each situation, sketch the graphs of the two functions on the same coordinate plane, so that <emphasis>S(t)</emphasis> is the height of the water in the small pool after <emphasis>t</emphasis> minutes, and <emphasis>L(t)</emphasis> is the height of the water in the large pool after <emphasis>t</emphasis> minutes.</para>
<para>In both functions, the height of the water is measured in inches.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="1" type="enumerated">
  <item>Situation 1: Each hose fills one pool at a constant rate. When the small pool is full, the water for that hose is shut off. The other hose keeps filling the larger pool until it is full.</item>
</list>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Sketch your interpretation of the graph of situation 1.</para>
  <para>When you have finished graphing, select the <emphasis>Solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <media><image alt="Two functions. time in minutes and height in inches." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3e7729067f9c62178fe62f7014cdf7f4166a434b"/></media></solution></exercise>
</example><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Situation 2: Each hose fills one pool at a constant rate. When the small pool is full, both hoses are shut off.</item>
</list>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Sketch your interpretation of the graph of situation 2.</para>
  <para>When you have finished graphing, select the <emphasis>Solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <media><image alt="Two functions. time in minutes and height in inches." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1c13b7c6a6e770635fbef0daca73a06e5aef3175"/></media></solution></exercise>
</example><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Situation 3: Each hose fills one pool at a constant rate. When the small pool is full, both hoses are used to fill the large pool until it is full.</item>
</list>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Sketch your interpretation of the graph of situation 3.</para>
  <para>When you have finished graphing, select the <emphasis>Solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <media><image alt="Two functions. time in minutes and height in inches." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8d57cf654267a72099f939d04b6907d86d948b88"/></media></solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
